# A function that runs often and names a top-level function tests whether the function object is there yet, and calls a stub where it is not. The stub makes a function object and changes no object that exists,
# so what the caller has read of its own list still holds behind it. The literal is longer than a batch, so it is allocated first and filled: its storage and its length are read once, not once an element
